# Environment Variables for Render Deployment

## Backend Environment Variables

Copy these to your Render backend service:

### Required Variables

```
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=8000
```

### Database
```
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/commentility?retryWrites=true&w=majority
```
**Note:** Replace with your MongoDB Atlas connection string

### CORS Configuration
```
CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend-url.onrender.com
```
**Note:** Update this after deploying frontend

### JWT Secrets
Generate random secrets using:
```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
```

```
ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=your_generated_secret_here
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY=1d
REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=your_different_generated_secret_here
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY=10d
```

### API Keys
```
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_youtube_api_key
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
```

### Cloudinary Configuration
```
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_api_secret
```

---

## Frontend Environment Variables

Copy these to your Render static site:

```
VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-url.onrender.com
```

---

## How to Get API Keys

### YouTube Data API v3
1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/)
2. Create a new project
3. Enable "YouTube Data API v3"
4. Create credentials (API Key)
5. Copy the API key

### Groq API
1. Go to [Groq Console](https://console.groq.com/)
2. Sign up / Log in
3. Navigate to API Keys
4. Create a new API key
5. Copy the key

### Cloudinary
1. Go to [Cloudinary](https://cloudinary.com/)
2. Sign up for free account
3. Go to Dashboard
4. Copy:
   - Cloud Name
   - API Key
   - API Secret

---

## Security Notes

> [!CAUTION]
> - Never commit these values to Git
> - Use different secrets for production and development
> - Rotate secrets regularly
> - Keep API keys secure
